    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Score as close to 88 points as possible (the par score). Players pay/receive based on deviation from 88. Alternatively, form valuable yaku combinations to stop play early and claim payment.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. Bidding Phase (if more than 3 players): Players bid to determine the 3 active players for the round. Non-active players sit out but may still earn from teyaku. 2. Dealing: Deal cards to the 3 active players. Place cards face-up in the center (the 'field'). 3. Playing Phase: Players take turns playing a card from hand to capture matching cards from the field. A card matches if it's from the same month/suit. After playing from hand, flip the top card from the deck. If it matches a field card, capture it. Captured cards go into the player's scoring pile. 4. Scoring: Total card points = 264 (par = 88 per player). Teyaku (Initial Hand Combinations): Declared before play for immediate payment. Deki-Yaku (Play Combinations): Formed during play. Player can stop early to claim payment. Final score = (Your points - 88). Positive = win, Negative = loss.",
